{"parentUuid":"2dfe8cdc-5483-406e-9e6d-b5b34ec4aefa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"edac4314-7853-44b7-9152-71a2296efc96","agentId":"adcc66282c1dd04fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hek2UPGJF1m1tErsEZxwg2","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntype: resource\ncreated: 2026-09-07\nsource: /brain-audit\ndomain: [second-brain, tooling]\ntags: [audit, four-cs, baseline]\nstatus: raw\n---\n\n# Brain Audit — 2026-09-07\n\nFirst run of `/brain-audit`. This is the **baseline row** in `_trend.md`.\nCompanion: `os-audit-2026-07-24-secondbrain.md` (45 days ago, the only prior audit).\n\n## Score — 67 / 100\n\n| C | Score | Why |\n|---|---:|---|\n| **Context** | 17 / 25 | Tier A strong (40 memories), `Knowledge/` fresh (2d), `USER.md` at 90% of cap. But `MEMORY.md` is at 100% (2502 / 2500) with no headroom, and **0 grill sessions** — the biggest evergreen decisions are still only in Eric's head. |\n| **Connections** | 22 / 25 | All three live sources inside window: meeting sync 4d, `portfolio.json` 8d, ledger 27d. Ledger is nearly out of its 30d window — the only thing holding this below 25. |\n| **Capabilities** | 15 / 25 | 161 skills installed. The July audit's `Knowledge/` segmentation finding **did** ship. But no audit→build loop existed until today, so most findings were never converted into anything. |\n| **Cadence** | 13 / 25 | All 9 launchd jobs `exit=0`. `Notes/` is 35 days stale — squarely in the 21–45d band. Green jobs, frozen synthesis. |\n\n**Rubric note:** Context scored 17 rather than the flat 13 the \"one file over cap\"\nanchor implies. `MEMORY.md` is over by 2 characters, not meaningfully bloated; the\n17 reflects the grill gap instead. Future runs: hold this interpretation.\n\n## Measured state\n\n| Folder | Files | Newest | Days stale |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n| `Inbox/` | 288 | 2026-09-07 | 0 |\n| `Knowledge/` | 421 | 2026-09-05 | 2 |\n| `Projects/` | 133 | 2026-08-11 | 27 |\n| `Notes/` | 23 | 2026-08-03 | 35 |\n| `Archive/` | 6 | 2026-07-30 | 39 |\n| `Drafts/` | 1 | 2026-07-31 | 38 |\n\n`Inbox/` is cron-fed and proves nothing. `Notes/` is the honest signal.\n\n## The three tests\n\n**1. Teammate test — WARN.** Sport-science references, meetings and papers are filed\nand retrievable through memsearch; a teammate question in that domain gets a better,\nsourced answer than memory. But the *reasoning* behind live decisions is not filed.\nKitman vs MyLink has no note behind it. The ATH Tech framework's five unwritten gaps\nare named but not explained.\n\n**2. Context-switch test — PASS.** Command centre at `localhost:7373`, the `/os`\nboard, and the portfolio dashboard cover the surface. Caveat: `portfolio.json` is\n8 days old, so the board is showing slightly stale state.\n\n**3. Head-emptying test — FAIL.** `MEMORY.md` → Pending Decisions carries the OKR Q1\ngate marked **DUE (was 8/31)** — seven days overdue — and Kitman vs MyLink still\nundecided with no supporting note. These are being re-held, not retrieved.\n\n## What would make the agent wrong-answer him today\n\n1. **`MEMORY.md` is at 100% of its cap.** The next write either truncates something or\n   silently fails. Working memory is the file with the highest read frequency in the\n   system, so this is the most expensive place to lose a fact.\n2. **Zero captured reasoning on the two live decisions.** Ask the system \"why are we\n   leaning MyLink?\" and it can only repeat the one-line cost comparison from\n   `MEMORY.md`. The actual argument does not exist on disk.\n3. **The synthesis half has now frozen twice.** 2026-06-05, restarted after the July\n   audit, frozen again 2026-08-03. Two data points make it a pattern, not an incident.\n\n## Level up — two builds\n\n### Build 1 — `/grill-me <topic>` → `Inbox/grills/`\n\nTargets **Context** (lowest real gap) and the failed head-emptying test.\n\n`interview-me` is day-driven. `mattpocock-skills:grilling` writes nothing to disk —\nit is 28 lines with no output step. Neither is \"interrogate me on one topic and file\nthe transcript.\"\n\nThis is also the build that matches the recorded bottleneck. `user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md`\nsays the limiting factor is the absence of a thinking partner, that ideation happens\nin company rather than in solitude, and that the right move is to *help him capture\nwhat surfaces*. A grill session is that outlet, and it leaves a file behind.\n\nFirst three topics, in order: the Kitman vs MyLink argument, the ATH Tech ITS blocker,\nthe OKR Q1 gate that is now overdue.\n\n### Build 2 — put `/brain-audit` on the rituals cadence, monthly\n\nTargets **Cadence**.\n\n`com.keystone.rituals` already exists and runs green. The measured history is\nunambiguous: every timer-driven part of this system is alive, and every manual part\nstopped within six weeks. A monthly audit that has to be remembered will not survive,\nand this file will look like `os-audit-2026-07-24` did — alone.\n\n## Next run\n\nMonthly. The number to watch is **Cadence**, and the single question is whether\n`Notes/` is under 21 days.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"82b30f3c-77fb-4864-b511-b05785f26b0f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:30:01.618Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\ntype: resource\ncreated: 2026-09-07\nsource: /brain-audit\ndomain: [second-brain, tooling]\ntags: [audit, four-cs, baseline]\nstatus: raw\n---\n\n# Brain Audit — 2026-09-07\n\nFirst run of `/brain-audit`. This is the **baseline row** in `_trend.md`.\nCompanion: `os-audit-2026-07-24-secondbrain.md` (45 days ago, the only prior audit).\n\n## Score — 67 / 100\n\n| C | Score | Why |\n|---|---:|---|\n| **Context** | 17 / 25 | Tier A strong (40 memories), `Knowledge/` fresh (2d), `USER.md` at 90% of cap. But `MEMORY.md` is at 100% (2502 / 2500) with no headroom, and **0 grill sessions** — the biggest evergreen decisions are still only in Eric's head. |\n| **Connections** | 22 / 25 | All three live sources inside window: meeting sync 4d, `portfolio.json` 8d, ledger 27d. Ledger is