\n1. **`MEMORY.md` is at 100% of its cap.** The next write either truncates something or\n   silently fails. Working memory is the file with the highest read frequency in the\n   system, so this is the most expensive place to lose a fact.\n2. **Zero captured reasoning on the two live decisions.** Ask the system \"why are we\n   leaning MyLink?\" and it can only repeat the one-line cost comparison from\n   `MEMORY.md`. The actual argument does not exist on disk.\n3. **The synthesis half has now frozen twice.** 2026-06-05, restarted after the July\n   audit, frozen again 2026-08-03. Two data points make it a pattern, not an incident.\n\n## Level up — two builds\n\n### Build 1 — `/grill-me <topic>` → `Inbox/grills/`\n\nTargets **Context** (lowest real gap) and the failed head-emptying test.\n\n`interview-me` is day-driven. `mattpocock-skills:grilling` writes nothing to disk —\nit is 28 lines with no output step. Neither is \"interrogate me on one topic and file\nthe transcript.\"\n\nThis is also the build that matches the recorded bottleneck. `user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md`\nsays the limiting factor is the absence of a thinking partner, that ideation happens\nin company rather than in solitude, and that the right move is to *help him capture\nwhat surfaces*. A grill session is that outlet, and it leaves a file behind.\n\nFirst three topics, in order: the Kitman vs MyLink argument, the ATH Tech ITS blocker,\nthe OKR Q1 gate that is now overdue.\n\n### Build 2 — put `/brain-audit` on the rituals cadence, monthly\n\nTargets **Cadence**.\n\n`com.keystone.rituals` already exists and runs green. The measured history is\nunambiguous: every timer-driven part of this system is alive, and every manual part\nstopped within six weeks. A monthly audit that has to be remembered will not survive,\nand this file will look like `os-audit-2026-07-24` did — alone.\n\n## Next run\n\nMonthly. The number to watch is **Cadence**, and the single question is whether\n`Notes/` is under 21 days.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2dfe8cdc-5483-406e-9e6d-b5b34ec4aefa","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
