{"parentUuid":"203f7d9c-2f11-4902-9c0e-bb208daac6d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"edac4314-7853-44b7-9152-71a2296efc96","agentId":"adcc66282c1dd04fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGqPoPSoYEcvG4VE1d3NgU","type":"tool_result","content":"== Kitman/MyLink notes\n== OKR gate notes\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/self-authored-direction.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/the-ask-has-to-precede-the-dependency.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/delivery-is-part-of-the-mechanism.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/planning-windows-compound.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/the-daily-on-ramp.md\n== recent interviews\n2026-07-27-interview.md\n2026-07-28-interview.md\n2026-07-29-interview.md\n2026-07-31-interview.md\n2026-08-03-interview.md\n2026-09-09-interview.md\n== command centre\n200\n== skill bloat memory\n---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n  modified: 2026-09-12T22:59:50.121Z\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"faf6abee-b4d0-4edc-96b2-883ca261fb6e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:30:28.301Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== Kitman/MyLink notes\n== OKR gate notes\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/self-authored-direction.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/the-ask-has-to-precede-the-dependency.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/delivery-is-part-of-the-mechanism.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/planning-windows-compound.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Notes/the-daily-on-ramp.md\n== recent interviews\n2026-07-27-interview.md\n2026-07-28-interview.md\n2026-07-29-interview.md\n2026-07-31-interview.md\n2026-08-03-interview.md\n2026-09-09-interview.md\n== command centre\n200\n== skill bloat memory\n---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n  modified: 2026-09-12T22:59:50.121Z\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"shared":true}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"203f7d9c-2f11-4902-9c0e-bb208daac6d6","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
